From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] hvf: a free page report gives the old pages back to macOS

Applies after qemu-hvf-free-page-reclaim.patch and
qemu-hvf-mapped-sections.patch (both left as they are).

What: hvf_report_free_pages() moves the reported range's old memory aside
(mach_vm_remap: one more mapping of the same pages, none touched) before the
fresh MAP_FIXED mapping takes its place (omacvm_reclaim_backing()). A
worker thread ("omacvm-reclaim", utility QoS) then advises the old range
MADV_FREE_REUSABLE and unmaps it (omacvm_reclaim_release()): macOS drops
its compressed copies at once and takes its resident pages first, without
compressing them. Pages macOS is compressing at that very moment are
skipped; the worker looks again 20 ms later and advises once more (twice at
most). A full queue (4096 ranges) releases in place; a range that cannot
move aside is advised in place; a refused madvise is logged once per run
and the replacement goes on as before. OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0: the
replacement alone, as up to 3.2.10.
qemu.log gets a line an hour while the guest reports, and one at exit:
reports, MB back to the Mac, blocks, how long the replacements held the
main lock per report (p99, longest), and what the releases left on the Mac.
OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK=1 (tests only): a line per report with what its range
held before the release and what it left after.

Why: MAP_FIXED alone only drops QEMU's mapping. XNU frees the pages of an
anonymous object when the whole object goes, and guest RAM is a few
128 MB objects that stay mapped around a reported range: the old pages
stayed resident or compressed, counted in no footprint, until QEMU quit.
A host test kept 1.0 of 1.0 GB "freed" until exit; a 4 GB VM after a
browser session still held 1.6 of the 3.3 GB it had reported, 88 % of it
compressed. Activity Monitor's figure for the VM falls either way; this is
memory it never showed. XNU applies the advice to a shared object only
when it is copy-delay (vm_map_reusable_pages); hv_vm_map makes guest RAM
exactly that (true share, ref >= 2), which the test checks first. The
advice costs about 0.1 ms per MB the Mac still holds (MacBook Air M2): up
to 10 ms per report when it ran under the main lock (MAP_FIXED alone:
3.2 ms), so it runs on the worker.

Upstream: OmacVM only (upstream QEMU discards a report with
madvise(MADV_DONTNEED), which keeps guest-dirtied pages on macOS).
Test: Tests/memory/test-reclaim.sh, no VM: guest RAM shared with a second
map or a real hv_vm_map, split by earlier reports; after each report and
its release the old pages are neither resident (unless reusable) nor
compressed, but for those macOS was compressing at that very moment (up to
5 % allowed), and the pages around keep their data. main's helper and
OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0 fail it (Mac mini, macOS 27, real hv_vm_map,
region compressed first: main left 4832 of 4848 pages compressed, the
advice 0). The runtime build runs it on the patched source, CI on this file.

--- a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
+++ b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
@@ -17,13 +17,18 @@
 #include "system/address-spaces.h"
 #include "system/memory.h"
 #include "system/ramblock.h"
+#include "system/system.h"
 #include "qemu/main-loop.h"
+#include "qemu/timer.h"
 #include "system/hvf.h"
 #include "system/hvf_int.h"
 #include "hw/core/cpu.h"
 #include "hw/core/boards.h"
 #include "trace.h"
 
+#include <mach/mach.h>
+#include <mach/mach_vm.h>
+
 bool hvf_allowed;
 bool hvf_kernel_irqchip;
 bool hvf_nested_virt;
@@ -160,6 +165,400 @@ static void hvf_set_phys_mem(MemoryRegionSection *section, bool add)
     g_hash_table_add(hvf_mapped_sections, g_memdup2(&gpa, sizeof(gpa)));
 }
 
+/* omacvm-reclaim: begin (app/runtime/Tests/memory/test-reclaim.sh builds this part alone) */
+/*
+ * Give the pages of a reported free range back to macOS.
+ *
+ * Darwin's MADV_DONTNEED keeps guest-dirtied RAM, so the range gets a fresh
+ * demand-zero mapping at the same address (MAP_FIXED: no unreserved gap).
+ * That alone only drops QEMU's mapping: macOS frees the pages of an
+ * anonymous object when the whole object goes, and guest RAM is a few large
+ * objects (128 MB each) that stay mapped around the range. The old pages
+ * stayed resident or compressed, counted in no footprint, until QEMU quit.
+ *
+ * So the old range first moves aside (one more mapping of the same memory,
+ * mach_vm_remap: no page is touched), and omacvm_reclaim_release() advises
+ * it MADV_FREE_REUSABLE and unmaps it, on a worker thread: macOS drops the
+ * compressed copies at once and takes the resident pages first, without
+ * compressing them. XNU does that for guest RAM, which the hypervisor's map
+ * shares (copy-delay, ref >= 2; Tests/memory/test-reclaim.c with a real
+ * hv_vm_map). The advice costs about 0.1 ms per MB the Mac still held (M2),
+ * up to 10 ms for one report: too long under the BQL. Pages macOS is
+ * compressing at that moment are skipped by the advice; the worker looks
+ * again 20 ms later and advises once more (twice at most). The guest
+ * touches none of these pages until QEMU acknowledges the report, and the
+ * fresh mapping takes the range before that, so the reusable state stays on
+ * pages that no guest mapping reaches again. Order: the stage-2 unmap (no
+ * vCPU reaches the range), the move aside, the new backing, the stage-2 map.
+ * OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0: the new backing alone, as up to 3.2.10.
+ */
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimPages {
+    uint64_t resident, compressed;       /* bytes the Mac still holds */
+} OmacvmReclaimPages;
+
+static int omacvm_reclaim_reusable = -1;
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_refused;
+
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_on(void)
+{
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_reusable < 0) {
+        const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE");
+        omacvm_reclaim_reusable = !(v && !strcmp(v, "0"));
+    }
+    return omacvm_reclaim_reusable;
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_refusal(int err)
+{
+    if (!__atomic_exchange_n(&omacvm_reclaim_refused, true, __ATOMIC_RELAXED)) {
+        warn_report("OmacVM: free page reporting: macOS refused to drop the "
+                    "old pages (%s); they stay on the Mac until QEMU quits",
+                    strerror(err));
+    }
+}
+
+/* What the Mac still holds of [at, at + size): resident and not reusable, or compressed. */
+static OmacvmReclaimPages omacvm_reclaim_held(mach_vm_address_t at, size_t size)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimPages held = { 0, 0 };
+    size_t page = (size_t)getpagesize();
+    int disp[256];
+    mach_vm_size_t off = 0, n, i;
+
+    while (off < size) {
+        n = (size - off) / page < 256 ? (size - off) / page : 256;
+        if (mach_vm_page_range_query(mach_task_self(), at + off, n * page,
+                                     (mach_vm_address_t)disp, &n) != KERN_SUCCESS || !n) {
+            break;
+        }
+        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+            if (disp[i] & VM_PAGE_QUERY_PAGE_PAGED_OUT) {
+                held.compressed += page;
+            } else if ((disp[i] & VM_PAGE_QUERY_PAGE_PRESENT) &&
+                       !(disp[i] & VM_PAGE_QUERY_PAGE_REUSABLE)) {
+                held.resident += page;
+            }
+        }
+        off += n * page;
+    }
+    return held;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Under the BQL: the new backing for a reported range. Returns the old range,
+ * moved aside, for omacvm_reclaim_release() (0: nothing to release).
+ */
+static mach_vm_address_t omacvm_reclaim_backing(hwaddr gpa, void *host,
+                                                size_t size,
+                                                hv_memory_flags_t flags)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t aside = 0;
+    vm_prot_t cur, max;
+    void *replacement;
+
+    trace_hvf_vm_unmap(gpa, size);
+    assert_hvf_ok(hv_vm_unmap(gpa, size));
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_on() &&
+        mach_vm_remap(mach_task_self(), &aside, size, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
+                      mach_task_self(), (mach_vm_address_t)host, FALSE,
+                      &cur, &max, VM_INHERIT_NONE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        /* No room to move it aside: the advice here, under the BQL. */
+        aside = 0;
+        if (madvise(host, size, MADV_FREE_REUSABLE) != 0) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_refusal(errno);
+        }
+    }
+    replacement = mmap(host, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
+                       MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0);
+    if (replacement == MAP_FAILED) {
+        error_report("HVF free-page backing replacement failed: %s",
+                     strerror(errno));
+        abort();
+    }
+    assert(replacement == host);
+    trace_hvf_vm_map(gpa, size, host, flags,
+                     flags & HV_MEMORY_READ ? 'R' : '-',
+                     flags & HV_MEMORY_WRITE ? 'W' : '-',
+                     flags & HV_MEMORY_EXEC ? 'X' : '-');
+    assert_hvf_ok(hv_vm_map(host, gpa, size, flags));
+    return aside;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The old range moved aside: advise it and unmap it. patient (the worker):
+ * pages still held 20 ms later are advised once more, twice at most. Returns
+ * what is still on the Mac after all; *before (when not NULL): what it held
+ * first.
+ */
+static OmacvmReclaimPages omacvm_reclaim_release(mach_vm_address_t aside,
+                                                 size_t size, bool patient,
+                                                 OmacvmReclaimPages *before)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimPages left = { 0, 0 };
+    int tries;
+
+    if (before) {
+        *before = omacvm_reclaim_held(aside, size);
+    }
+    for (tries = 0; tries < (patient ? 3 : 1); tries++) {
+        if (tries) {
+            usleep(20000);
+        }
+        if (madvise((void *)aside, size, MADV_FREE_REUSABLE) != 0) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_refusal(errno);
+            patient = false;            /* no point in asking again */
+        }
+        if (!patient && !before) {
+            break;
+        }
+        left = omacvm_reclaim_held(aside, size);
+        if (!patient || (!left.resident && !left.compressed)) {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    munmap((void *)aside, size);
+    return left;
+}
+/* omacvm-reclaim: end */
+
+/*
+ * The worker: releases the ranges moved aside, in order, at utility QoS. A
+ * full queue (the guest reports faster than it releases) releases in place.
+ * A marker item (aside 0) closes a report for OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK's line.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE 4096
+
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimItem {
+    mach_vm_address_t aside;
+    size_t size;
+    int64_t hold_ns;                    /* a marker: the report's hold */
+} OmacvmReclaimItem;
+
+static struct {
+    QemuMutex lock;
+    QemuCond more;
+    QemuThread thread;
+    bool started;
+    unsigned head, count;
+    OmacvmReclaimItem item[OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE];
+    /* under lock: what the releases left (OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK: and held) */
+    uint64_t released, in_place, left_resident, left_compressed;
+    uint64_t held_before, compressed_before;
+} omacvm_reclaim_w;
+
+/*
+ * What free page reporting gave back, for qemu.log: a line an hour while the
+ * guest reports, and one at exit. A report is one virtqueue element (Linux
+ * sends up to 32 blocks and waits for each); its hold is the time its blocks'
+ * unmap, move aside, new backing and map kept the BQL. Under the BQL.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS 100000     /* hold histogram: 0.1 ms steps */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS 400          /* the last one counts 40 ms and up */
+
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimStats {
+    uint64_t reports, blocks, bytes;
+    int64_t longest_ns;
+    uint32_t hold[OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS];
+} OmacvmReclaimStats;
+
+static struct {
+    uint64_t blocks, bytes, queued;
+    int64_t ns;
+} omacvm_reclaim_cur;
+static OmacvmReclaimStats omacvm_reclaim_hour, omacvm_reclaim_run;
+static int64_t omacvm_reclaim_hour_start;
+static int omacvm_reclaim_check = -1;
+static Notifier omacvm_reclaim_exit;
+
+/* OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK=1 (tests only): a line per report with what it left on the Mac. */
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_check_on(void)
+{
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_check < 0) {
+        const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK");
+        omacvm_reclaim_check = v && !strcmp(v, "1");
+    }
+    return omacvm_reclaim_check;
+}
+
+static double omacvm_reclaim_mb(uint64_t bytes)
+{
+    return bytes / (1024.0 * 1024.0);
+}
+
+static void *omacvm_reclaim_work(void *opaque)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimItem it;
+    OmacvmReclaimPages before = { 0, 0 }, left, rb = { 0, 0 }, rl = { 0, 0 };
+    uint64_t blocks = 0, bytes = 0;
+    bool check = omacvm_reclaim_check_on();
+
+    pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_UTILITY, 0);
+    for (;;) {
+        qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        while (!omacvm_reclaim_w.count) {
+            qemu_cond_wait(&omacvm_reclaim_w.more, &omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        }
+        it = omacvm_reclaim_w.item[omacvm_reclaim_w.head];
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.head = (omacvm_reclaim_w.head + 1) % OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE;
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.count--;
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        if (!it.aside) {
+            if (check && blocks) {
+                info_report("OmacVM: reclaim check: %" PRIu64 " blocks, %.1f MB: "
+                            "%.1f MB held before (%.1f MB compressed), %.1f MB "
+                            "left resident, %.1f MB left compressed; hold %.2f ms",
+                            blocks, omacvm_reclaim_mb(bytes),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rb.resident + rb.compressed),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rb.compressed),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rl.resident),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rl.compressed), it.hold_ns / 1e6);
+            }
+            blocks = bytes = 0;
+            rb = rl = (OmacvmReclaimPages) { 0, 0 };
+            continue;
+        }
+        left = omacvm_reclaim_release(it.aside, it.size, true, check ? &before : NULL);
+        qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.released += it.size;
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.left_resident += left.resident;
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.left_compressed += left.compressed;
+        if (check) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_w.held_before += before.resident + before.compressed;
+            omacvm_reclaim_w.compressed_before += before.compressed;
+        }
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        if (check) {
+            blocks++;
+            bytes += it.size;
+            rb.resident += before.resident;
+            rb.compressed += before.compressed;
+            rl.resident += left.resident;
+            rl.compressed += left.compressed;
+        }
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+/* Under the BQL. */
+static void omacvm_reclaim_queue(mach_vm_address_t aside, size_t size,
+                                 int64_t hold_ns)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimItem *it;
+
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_w.started) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.started = true;
+        qemu_mutex_init(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        qemu_cond_init(&omacvm_reclaim_w.more);
+        qemu_thread_create(&omacvm_reclaim_w.thread, "omacvm-reclaim",
+                           omacvm_reclaim_work, NULL, QEMU_THREAD_DETACHED);
+    }
+    qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_w.count == OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.in_place += aside ? 1 : 0;
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        if (aside) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_release(aside, size, false, NULL);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+    it = &omacvm_reclaim_w.item[(omacvm_reclaim_w.head + omacvm_reclaim_w.count) %
+                                OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE];
+    it->aside = aside;
+    it->size = size;
+    it->hold_ns = hold_ns;
+    omacvm_reclaim_w.count++;
+    qemu_cond_signal(&omacvm_reclaim_w.more);
+    qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_log(const char *when, const OmacvmReclaimStats *s)
+{
+    uint64_t need = s->reports - s->reports / 100, seen = 0;
+    g_autofree char *left = NULL;
+    int step;
+
+    if (!s->reports) {
+        return;
+    }
+    for (step = 0; step < OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1; step++) {
+        seen += s->hold[step];
+        if (seen >= need) {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_w.started) {
+        qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        left = g_strdup_printf("; this run %.0f MB released, %.0f MB of it left "
+                               "on the Mac (%.0f resident, %.0f compressed)%s",
+                               omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.released),
+                               omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.left_resident +
+                                                 omacvm_reclaim_w.left_compressed),
+                               omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.left_resident),
+                               omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.left_compressed),
+                               omacvm_reclaim_w.in_place ? ", some released in place" : "");
+        if (omacvm_reclaim_check_on()) {
+            char *c = g_strdup_printf("%s; check: %.0f MB held before (%.0f MB "
+                                      "compressed)", left,
+                                      omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.held_before),
+                                      omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.compressed_before));
+            g_free(left);
+            left = c;
+        }
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    }
+    info_report("OmacVM: free page reporting %s: %" PRIu64 " reports, %.0f MB "
+                "back to the Mac (%" PRIu64 " blocks%s); main lock held p99 "
+                "%.1f ms, longest %.1f ms%s", when, s->reports,
+                omacvm_reclaim_mb(s->bytes), s->blocks,
+                omacvm_reclaim_reusable == 0 ?
+                ", old pages left in place: OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0" : "",
+                (step + 1) * OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS / 1e6,
+                s->longest_ns / 1e6, left ? left : "");
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_at_exit(Notifier *n, void *data)
+{
+    omacvm_reclaim_log("this run", &omacvm_reclaim_run);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_add(OmacvmReclaimStats *s, int step)
+{
+    s->reports++;
+    s->blocks += omacvm_reclaim_cur.blocks;
+    s->bytes += omacvm_reclaim_cur.bytes;
+    s->longest_ns = MAX(s->longest_ns, omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns);
+    s->hold[step]++;
+}
+
+void hvf_report_free_pages_done(void)
+{
+    int64_t now = get_clock();
+    int step;
+
+    assert(bql_locked());
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_cur.blocks) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_hour_start) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_hour_start = now;
+        omacvm_reclaim_exit.notify = omacvm_reclaim_at_exit;
+        qemu_add_exit_notifier(&omacvm_reclaim_exit);
+    }
+    step = MIN(omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns / OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS,
+               OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1);
+    omacvm_reclaim_add(&omacvm_reclaim_hour, step);
+    omacvm_reclaim_add(&omacvm_reclaim_run, step);
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_check_on() && omacvm_reclaim_cur.queued) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_queue(0, 0, omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns);
+    }
+    memset(&omacvm_reclaim_cur, 0, sizeof(omacvm_reclaim_cur));
+    if (now - omacvm_reclaim_hour_start >= 3600 * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_log("in the last hour", &omacvm_reclaim_hour);
+        memset(&omacvm_reclaim_hour, 0, sizeof(omacvm_reclaim_hour));
+        omacvm_reclaim_hour_start = now;
+    }
+}
+
 void hvf_report_free_pages(hwaddr gpa, void *host, size_t size)
 {
     MemoryRegionSection section;
@@ -167,7 +566,8 @@ void hvf_report_free_pages(hwaddr gpa, void *host, size_t size)
     RAMBlock *rb;
     size_t page_size = qemu_real_host_page_size();
     hv_memory_flags_t flags = HV_MEMORY_READ | HV_MEMORY_WRITE | HV_MEMORY_EXEC;
-    void *replacement;
+    mach_vm_address_t aside;
+    int64_t start;
 
     assert(bql_locked());
     if (!size || !QEMU_IS_ALIGNED(gpa | (uintptr_t)host | size, page_size)) {
@@ -195,28 +595,16 @@ void hvf_report_free_pages(hwaddr gpa, void *host, size_t size)
         return;
     }
 
-    /* Darwin MADV_DONTNEED does not discard guest-dirtied RAM. First remove
-     * the stage-2 mapping, then replace its host backing with fresh demand-zero
-     * pages at the same address. MAP_FIXED avoids any unreserved-address gap.
-     * Unlike MADV_FREE_REUSABLE, this uses public APIs and leaves no reusable
-     * accounting state on pages that the guest subsequently allocates again.
-     * The guest owns none of these pages until we acknowledge its report.
-     */
-    trace_hvf_vm_unmap(gpa, size);
-    assert_hvf_ok(hv_vm_unmap(gpa, size));
-    replacement = mmap(host, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
-                       MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0);
-    if (replacement == MAP_FAILED) {
-        error_report("HVF free-page backing replacement failed: %s",
-                     strerror(errno));
-        abort();
+    /* The guest owns none of these pages until we acknowledge its report. */
+    start = get_clock();
+    aside = omacvm_reclaim_backing(gpa, host, size, flags);
+    omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns += get_clock() - start;
+    omacvm_reclaim_cur.blocks++;
+    omacvm_reclaim_cur.bytes += size;
+    if (aside) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_queue(aside, size, 0);
+        omacvm_reclaim_cur.queued++;
     }
-    assert(replacement == host);
-    trace_hvf_vm_map(gpa, size, host, flags,
-                     flags & HV_MEMORY_READ ? 'R' : '-',
-                     flags & HV_MEMORY_WRITE ? 'W' : '-',
-                     flags & HV_MEMORY_EXEC ? 'X' : '-');
-    assert_hvf_ok(hv_vm_map(host, gpa, size, flags));
     memory_region_unref(mr);
 }
 
--- a/accel/stubs/hvf-stub.c
+++ b/accel/stubs/hvf-stub.c
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@ void hvf_report_free_pages(hwaddr gpa, void *host, size_t size)
     g_assert_not_reached();
 }
 
+void hvf_report_free_pages_done(void)
+{
+    g_assert_not_reached();
+}
+
